{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cg2hnXES61qHKBNnzGyZ1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WuM9zELVLDP8GEKQCpiRfA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/taskspec chat 7lxq8syy/.taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml","content":"schema_version: 1\n\nintent:\n  id: INT-RATE-LIMITING\n  title: Rate-limiting steel thread\n  summary: >-\n    Deliver the four-step rate-limiting steel thread stated in the blueprint:\n    a versioned policy schema that rejects invalid limits and windows, resolution\n    to exactly one effective policy per organization, denial of request 101 after\n    100 allowed requests in the same window, and a stable denial reason with\n    matching decision telemetry. Provider-owned usage metering stays outside this\n    boundary; production storage and deployment infrastructure are not selected\n    by this plan.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: \"2026-10-14T19:44:37Z\"\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n    - Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering, including any read, write, or reconciliation\n      of provider metering counters.\n    - Selection of production storage for window accounting.\n    - Selection of deployment infrastructure or rollout mechanism.\n\nsystem_map:\n  claim: derived\n  components:\n    - Policy schema and validation of limits and windows.\n    - Policy resolution producing one effective policy per organization.\n    - Window accounting and allow/deny decision for a request.\n    - Denial reason contract and decision telemetry emission.\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering (out of scope; this plan neither reads nor\n      writes it and must not become a second metering source of truth).\n  unknowns:\n    - No responsible owner is named for any in-scope seam. The blueprint states\n      only that usage metering is provider-owned; it assigns no owner for policy,\n      resolution, enforcement, or telemetry.\n    - The counter substrate for window accounting is unselected. The blueprint\n      declares production storage out of scope, yet step 3 requires counting 100\n      requests within a shared window.\n    - No implementation surface exists in this repository. There is no source\n      tree, language, or runtime established for the steel thread, so leaf\n      touches_paths and evals are proposed targets, not observed ones.\n    - The telemetry sink and the stability contract for the denial reason\n      (enumerated code versus free text) are unspecified.\n\nevidence:\n  - id: EV-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: proposed\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: \"2026-10-14T19:44:37Z\"\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 1\n    summary: >-\n      Blueprint stating the four-step steel thread order and the two boundaries:\n      provider-owned usage metering is out of scope, and production storage and\n      deployment infrastructure are not selected here. Digest verified locally.\n  - id: EV-EMPTY-WORKSPACE\n    claim: current\n    source:\n      uri: tasks/.gitkeep\n      captured_at: \"2026-10-14T19:44:37Z\"\n      sha256: e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\n    confidence: 1\n    summary: >-\n      The workspace holds no tasks, no plans, and no implementation source tree.\n      Every leaf below creates new surface rather than modifying observed code.\n\ndecisions:\n  - id: D-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    status: accepted\n    owner: blueprint\n    rationale: >-\n      Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope. Rate-limit window\n      accounting is a separate concern from provider metering and must not read,\n      write, or reconcile provider metering counters.\n  - id: D-COUNTER-STORE\n    status: proposed\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    rationale: >-\n      Window accounting needs a counter substrate, but the blueprint declares\n      production storage unselected. Unresolved: whether the steel thread proves\n      denial against an in-process reference counter behind a port, or whether a\n      shared store is selected first. This decision is not taken by this plan.\n  - id: D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n    status: proposed\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    rationale: >-\n      No owner is named for the in-scope seams. Seam and swimlane owners below\n      are recorded as UNASSIGNED to preserve the gap rather than invent an owner.\n\nseams:\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-SCHEMA\n    name: Policy schema and validation\n    description: >-\n      Versioned schema for rate-limit policies that rejects invalid limits and\n      windows at the boundary, before any policy is stored or resolved.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Own the policy document shape and its validity rules, including version\n      identity and rejection of invalid limits and windows.\n    consumes:\n      - candidate policy document\n    produces:\n      - validated versioned policy\n      - schema validation errors\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Valid and invalid policy fixtures are validated directly against the\n      schema, with no resolution, enforcement, or telemetry involved.\n    decision_ids:\n      - D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Validate limits and windows inside the enforcement path.\n        reason: >-\n          Defers rejection of invalid policy to request time and leaves step 1 of\n          the steel thread without independent proof.\n      - alternative: Unversioned policy shape.\n        reason: >-\n          The blueprint requires a versioned schema; without version identity,\n          resolution cannot state which policy revision was effective.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-SCHEMA\n      name: Policy schema\n      owner: UNASSIGNED\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-SCHEMA-REJECTS-INVALID\n          observable_state: >-\n            A versioned policy schema accepts valid policies and rejects invalid\n            limits and windows with a named validation error.\n          proof: >-\n            Fixture-driven validation suite over valid and invalid policy\n            documents, asserting accept and reject outcomes and error identity.\n          requires: []\n          produces:\n            - validated versioned policy\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-policy-schema\n              title: Versioned rate-limit policy schema with validation\n              goal: >-\n                Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema and a validator\n                that rejects invalid limits and windows with named errors.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Valid policy fixtures validate successfully; policies with\n                non-positive, non-integer, or missing limits and with missing or\n                non-positive windows are rejected with a named validation error;\n                the schema carries an explicit version field.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on: []\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema\n                - tests/ratelimit/policy_schema\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A policy document with a positive integer limit and a positive window.\n                  when: The document is validated against the versioned schema.\n                  then: Validation succeeds and reports the schema version.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: A policy document with a non-positive or missing limit or window.\n                  when: The document is validated against the versioned schema.\n                  then: Validation fails with a named error identifying the invalid field.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Valid policy fixtures are accepted and report a schema version.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/policy_schema/run.sh valid\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Invalid limit and window fixtures are rejected with named errors.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/policy_schema/run.sh invalid\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Schema version field is present and explicitly asserted.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/policy_schema/run.sh version\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading or writing provider usage metering counters.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope for this\n                    initiative.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Keep this leaf confined to policy document shape and validity.\n                - action: Selecting a production storage engine for policies.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Production storage is explicitly not selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Validate documents in memory from fixtures and leave\n                    persistence to the unresolved D-COUNTER-STORE decision.\n                - action: Implementing resolution or enforcement in this leaf.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Those are separate seams with their own independent proof.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Produce only the validated versioned policy contract.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created schema and test paths.\n              observability: Validation errors are named and enumerable.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - design\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n    name: Effective policy resolution\n    description: >-\n      Deterministic reduction of applicable policies to exactly one effective\n      policy for an organization at a point in time.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Own precedence and tie-breaking so that resolution is total and\n      single-valued for an organization.\n    consumes:\n      - validated versioned policy\n      - organization identifier\n    produces:\n      - exactly one effective policy per organization\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Resolution is exercised over overlapping and conflicting policy sets and\n      asserted to yield exactly one effective policy, without invoking\n      enforcement or telemetry.\n    decision_ids:\n      - D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Let the enforcement path pick the first matching policy.\n        reason: >-\n          Makes the effective policy an implicit side effect of iteration order\n          and leaves step 2 of the steel thread unprovable on its own.\n      - alternative: Allow resolution to return multiple candidate policies.\n        reason: >-\n          The blueprint requires exactly one effective policy per organization.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n      name: Policy resolution\n      owner: UNASSIGNED\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-ONE-EFFECTIVE-POLICY\n          observable_state: >-\n            For any organization and any set of validated policies, resolution\n            returns exactly one effective policy or an explicit no-policy result.\n          proof: >-\n            Resolution tests over overlapping, conflicting, and empty policy sets\n            assert single-valued, deterministic outcomes.\n          requires:\n            - validated versioned policy\n          produces:\n            - exactly one effective policy per organization\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-policy-resolution\n              title: Deterministic effective-policy resolution per organization\n              goal: >-\n                Resolve a validated policy set to exactly one effective policy\n                for an organization using declared precedence and tie-breaking.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Resolution over overlapping and conflicting policy sets returns\n                exactly one effective policy; an empty set returns an explicit\n                no-policy result; repeated resolution of the same input is\n                identical.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20261014-policy-schema\n              touches_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/resolution\n                - tests/ratelimit/resolution\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: An organization with several overlapping validated policies.\n                  when: Effective policy resolution runs.\n                  then: Exactly one effective policy is returned, chosen by declared precedence.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: An organization with no applicable policy.\n                  when: Effective policy resolution runs.\n                  then: An explicit no-policy result is returned rather than a default or an error.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Overlapping policy sets resolve to exactly one effective policy.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/resolution/run.sh overlapping\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Empty and non-matching sets return an explicit no-policy result.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/resolution/run.sh empty\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Resolution is deterministic across repeated and reordered input.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/resolution/run.sh deterministic\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Deriving precedence from provider metering or plan usage data.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Derive precedence only from declared policy fields.\n                - action: Persisting resolved policies to a chosen production store.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Production storage is not selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Resolve in memory over supplied validated policies.\n                - action: Returning a silent default policy when none applies.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Hides the no-policy case and makes the single-valued claim\n                    untestable.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Return an explicit no-policy result.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created resolution and test paths.\n              observability: Resolution records the chosen policy version and precedence reason.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - design\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-DECISION\n    name: Window accounting and denial decision\n    description: >-\n      Counting of requests within a window against the effective policy, the\n      allow or deny decision, the stable denial reason, and the matching\n      decision telemetry.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Own the per-window request count, the allow/deny outcome, the denial\n      reason contract, and emission of decision telemetry that matches the\n      returned decision.\n    consumes:\n      - exactly one effective policy per organization\n      - request event\n    produces:\n      - allow or deny decision\n      - stable denial reason\n      - decision telemetry event\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    independent_proof: >-\n      A 101-request sequence against a limit of 100 in one window asserts the\n      first 100 allowed and the 101st denied, and the emitted telemetry is\n      asserted to match the returned decision and reason.\n    decision_ids:\n      - D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n      - D-COUNTER-STORE\n      - D-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Derive the request count from provider usage metering.\n        reason: >-\n          Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope; reusing it would\n          make this seam a second consumer of a boundary the blueprint excludes.\n      - alternative: Emit telemetry from a separate asynchronous reconciliation job.\n        reason: >-\n          The blueprint requires the denial to emit matching telemetry, which a\n          decoupled job cannot prove within this thread.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-DECISION\n      name: Decision and telemetry\n      owner: UNASSIGNED\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-WINDOW-DENIAL\n          observable_state: >-\n            With an effective limit of 100 in a window, requests 1 through 100\n            are allowed and request 101 in the same window is denied.\n          proof: >-\n            Sequence test issuing 101 requests in one window asserting the\n            allow/deny boundary exactly at 101, and a window-rollover case.\n          requires:\n            - exactly one effective policy per organization\n          produces:\n            - allow or deny decision\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-window-decision\n              title: Window accounting and allow/deny decision at the policy limit\n              goal: >-\n                Count requests per organization within the policy window and deny\n                the first request that exceeds the effective limit.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Requests 1 through 100 are allowed and request 101 in the same\n                window is denied for a limit of 100; a request in the next window\n                is allowed again; counting goes through a port with no provider\n                metering dependency.\n              effort: M\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20261014-policy-resolution\n              touches_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/resolution\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/decision\n                - tests/ratelimit/decision\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: An organization with an effective limit of 100 in the current window.\n                  when: 101 requests are issued within that window.\n                  then: The first 100 are allowed and the 101st is denied.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: An organization that was denied in the previous window.\n                  when: A request arrives in the next window.\n                  then: The request is allowed because the window count has reset.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed in the same window.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/decision/run.sh boundary\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Window rollover resets the count and allows the next request.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/decision/run.sh rollover\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Counting depends only on the counter port, not provider metering.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/decision/run.sh counter-port-isolation\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading provider usage metering counters to decide allow or deny.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope; the\n                    decision must not depend on it.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Count through the rate-limit counter port owned by this seam.\n                - action: Committing to a production counter store in this leaf.\n                  reason: >-\n                    D-COUNTER-STORE is unresolved and production storage is not\n                    selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Depend on a counter port and stop for the decision if a\n                    durable store is required to finish.\n                - action: Widening the denial to other quota or billing concerns.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Only the rate-limit decision is in scope for this thread.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Return a rate-limit decision and leave other quotas alone.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created decision and test paths.\n              observability: Each decision records organization, window, count, and outcome.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              shared_resources:\n                - ratelimit-counter-port\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\n        - id: LEG-DENIAL-TELEMETRY\n          observable_state: >-\n            A denial returns a stable reason identifier and emits exactly one\n            decision telemetry event whose fields match the returned decision.\n          proof: >-\n            Denial test asserting the reason identifier is stable across runs\n            and that the captured telemetry event matches the returned decision.\n          requires:\n            - allow or deny decision\n          produces:\n            - stable denial reason\n            - decision telemetry event\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-denial-telemetry\n              title: Stable denial reason and matching decision telemetry\n              goal: >-\n                Return a stable denial reason identifier and emit one decision\n                telemetry event that matches the returned decision.\n              done_condition: >-\n                A denial returns an enumerated, stable reason identifier;\n                exactly one telemetry event is emitted per decision; the event\n                fields match the returned decision and reason; telemetry carries\n                no provider metering fields.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20261014-window-decision\n              touches_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/decision\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/telemetry\n                - tests/ratelimit/telemetry\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A request denied for exceeding the effective limit.\n                  when: The decision is returned.\n                  then: The response carries an enumerated denial reason that is stable across runs.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: Any allow or deny decision.\n                  when: The decision is returned.\n                  then: Exactly one telemetry event is emitted whose fields match the decision.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Denial reason is enumerated and stable across repeated runs.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/telemetry/run.sh stable-reason\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Exactly one telemetry event per decision, matching the outcome.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/telemetry/run.sh event-match\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Telemetry carries no provider metering fields.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/telemetry/run.sh no-metering-fields\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Emitting telemetry into the provider usage metering pipeline.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned; decision telemetry must not\n                    become a metering feed.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Emit to the decision telemetry sink owned by this seam.\n                - action: Returning free-text denial messages.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Free text is not a stable reason and cannot be asserted.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Return an enumerated reason identifier.\n                - action: Selecting a production telemetry backend.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Deployment infrastructure is not selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Emit through a sink port captured in tests.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created telemetry and test paths.\n              observability: Decision telemetry is the observability surface for this thread.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\nsteel_thread:\n  - LEG-SCHEMA-REJECTS-INVALID\n  - LEG-ONE-EFFECTIVE-POLICY\n  - LEG-WINDOW-DENIAL\n  - LEG-DENIAL-TELEMETRY\n\nobjections:\n  - id: OBJ-NO-SEAM-OWNER\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      No responsible owner is named for any in-scope seam or swimlane. Owners are\n      recorded as UNASSIGNED. The blueprint states only that usage metering is\n      provider-owned, which assigns nothing for policy, resolution, enforcement,\n      or telemetry. Ownership must be supplied by an explicit decision.\n  - id: OBJ-COUNTER-STORE-UNSELECTED\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      Steel thread step 3 requires counting 100 requests within a shared window,\n      but the blueprint declares production storage out of scope and unselected.\n      T-20261014-window-decision cannot reach a durable done condition until\n      D-COUNTER-STORE states whether the thread is proved against an in-process\n      reference counter behind a port or against a selected shared store.\n  - id: OBJ-NO-IMPLEMENTATION-SURFACE\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The repository contains no source tree, language, or runtime for the steel\n      thread. All touches_paths, creates_paths, and eval commands above are\n      proposed targets derived from the blueprint, not observed code. They\n      require confirmation against the real implementation repository before any\n      leaf is sealed.\n  - id: OBJ-REASON-CONTRACT-UNSPECIFIED\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The blueprint requires a stable denial reason but does not define the\n      stability contract or the telemetry sink. This plan proposes an enumerated\n      reason identifier and a sink port; both need confirmation.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3080,"cache_read_input_tokens":26931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3080,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b797ae4-2efc-430c-9d86-23005f3cd343","uuid":"cb16d16d-fe0b-45d9-819b-e65eb75d5377","timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:46:50.506Z","request_id":"req_011Cg2hnWsc3ZbsMSHFRcBQN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WuM9zELVLDP8GEKQCpiRfA":{"file_path":"/tmp/taskspec chat 7lxq8syy/.taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml","content":"schema_version: 1\n\nintent:\n  id: INT-RATE-LIMITING\n  title: Rate-limiting steel thread\n  summary: >-\n    Deliver the four-step rate-limiting steel thread stated in the blueprint:\n    a versioned policy schema that rejects invalid limits and windows, resolution\n    to exactly one effective policy per organization, denial of request 101 after\n    100 allowed requests in the same window, and a stable denial reason with\n    matching decision telemetry. Provider-owned usage metering stays outside this\n    boundary; production storage and deployment infrastructure are not selected\n    by this plan.\n  claim: proposed\n  source:\n    uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n    captured_at: \"2026-10-14T19:44:37Z\"\n    sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n  success:\n    - A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n    - Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n    - Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n    - The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n  out_of_scope:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering, including any read, write, or reconciliation\n      of provider metering counters.\n    - Selection of production storage for window accounting.\n    - Selection of deployment infrastructure or rollout mechanism.\n\nsystem_map:\n  claim: derived\n  components:\n    - Policy schema and validation of limits and windows.\n    - Policy resolution producing one effective policy per organization.\n    - Window accounting and allow/deny decision for a request.\n    - Denial reason contract and decision telemetry emission.\n  external_dependencies:\n    - Provider-owned usage metering (out of scope; this plan neither reads nor\n      writes it and must not become a second metering source of truth).\n  unknowns:\n    - No responsible owner is named for any in-scope seam. The blueprint states\n      only that usage metering is provider-owned; it assigns no owner for policy,\n      resolution, enforcement, or telemetry.\n    - The counter substrate for window accounting is unselected. The blueprint\n      declares production storage out of scope, yet step 3 requires counting 100\n      requests within a shared window.\n    - No implementation surface exists in this repository. There is no source\n      tree, language, or runtime established for the steel thread, so leaf\n      touches_paths and evals are proposed targets, not observed ones.\n    - The telemetry sink and the stability contract for the denial reason\n      (enumerated code versus free text) are unspecified.\n\nevidence:\n  - id: EV-BLUEPRINT\n    claim: proposed\n    source:\n      uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      captured_at: \"2026-10-14T19:44:37Z\"\n      sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n    confidence: 1\n    summary: >-\n      Blueprint stating the four-step steel thread order and the two boundaries:\n      provider-owned usage metering is out of scope, and production storage and\n      deployment infrastructure are not selected here. Digest verified locally.\n  - id: EV-EMPTY-WORKSPACE\n    claim: current\n    source:\n      uri: tasks/.gitkeep\n      captured_at: \"2026-10-14T19:44:37Z\"\n      sha256: e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\n    confidence: 1\n    summary: >-\n      The workspace holds no tasks, no plans, and no implementation source tree.\n      Every leaf below creates new surface rather than modifying observed code.\n\ndecisions:\n  - id: D-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    status: accepted\n    owner: blueprint\n    rationale: >-\n      Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope. Rate-limit window\n      accounting is a separate concern from provider metering and must not read,\n      write, or reconcile provider metering counters.\n  - id: D-COUNTER-STORE\n    status: proposed\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    rationale: >-\n      Window accounting needs a counter substrate, but the blueprint declares\n      production storage unselected. Unresolved: whether the steel thread proves\n      denial against an in-process reference counter behind a port, or whether a\n      shared store is selected first. This decision is not taken by this plan.\n  - id: D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n    status: proposed\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    rationale: >-\n      No owner is named for the in-scope seams. Seam and swimlane owners below\n      are recorded as UNASSIGNED to preserve the gap rather than invent an owner.\n\nseams:\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-SCHEMA\n    name: Policy schema and validation\n    description: >-\n      Versioned schema for rate-limit policies that rejects invalid limits and\n      windows at the boundary, before any policy is stored or resolved.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Own the policy document shape and its validity rules, including version\n      identity and rejection of invalid limits and windows.\n    consumes:\n      - candidate policy document\n    produces:\n      - validated versioned policy\n      - schema validation errors\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Valid and invalid policy fixtures are validated directly against the\n      schema, with no resolution, enforcement, or telemetry involved.\n    decision_ids:\n      - D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Validate limits and windows inside the enforcement path.\n        reason: >-\n          Defers rejection of invalid policy to request time and leaves step 1 of\n          the steel thread without independent proof.\n      - alternative: Unversioned policy shape.\n        reason: >-\n          The blueprint requires a versioned schema; without version identity,\n          resolution cannot state which policy revision was effective.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-SCHEMA\n      name: Policy schema\n      owner: UNASSIGNED\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-SCHEMA-REJECTS-INVALID\n          observable_state: >-\n            A versioned policy schema accepts valid policies and rejects invalid\n            limits and windows with a named validation error.\n          proof: >-\n            Fixture-driven validation suite over valid and invalid policy\n            documents, asserting accept and reject outcomes and error identity.\n          requires: []\n          produces:\n            - validated versioned policy\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-policy-schema\n              title: Versioned rate-limit policy schema with validation\n              goal: >-\n                Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema and a validator\n                that rejects invalid limits and windows with named errors.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Valid policy fixtures validate successfully; policies with\n                non-positive, non-integer, or missing limits and with missing or\n                non-positive windows are rejected with a named validation error;\n                the schema carries an explicit version field.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on: []\n              touches_paths: []\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema\n                - tests/ratelimit/policy_schema\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A policy document with a positive integer limit and a positive window.\n                  when: The document is validated against the versioned schema.\n                  then: Validation succeeds and reports the schema version.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: A policy document with a non-positive or missing limit or window.\n                  when: The document is validated against the versioned schema.\n                  then: Validation fails with a named error identifying the invalid field.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Valid policy fixtures are accepted and report a schema version.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/policy_schema/run.sh valid\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Invalid limit and window fixtures are rejected with named errors.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/policy_schema/run.sh invalid\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Schema version field is present and explicitly asserted.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/policy_schema/run.sh version\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading or writing provider usage metering counters.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope for this\n                    initiative.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Keep this leaf confined to policy document shape and validity.\n                - action: Selecting a production storage engine for policies.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Production storage is explicitly not selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Validate documents in memory from fixtures and leave\n                    persistence to the unresolved D-COUNTER-STORE decision.\n                - action: Implementing resolution or enforcement in this leaf.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Those are separate seams with their own independent proof.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Produce only the validated versioned policy contract.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created schema and test paths.\n              observability: Validation errors are named and enumerable.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - design\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n    name: Effective policy resolution\n    description: >-\n      Deterministic reduction of applicable policies to exactly one effective\n      policy for an organization at a point in time.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Own precedence and tie-breaking so that resolution is total and\n      single-valued for an organization.\n    consumes:\n      - validated versioned policy\n      - organization identifier\n    produces:\n      - exactly one effective policy per organization\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    independent_proof: >-\n      Resolution is exercised over overlapping and conflicting policy sets and\n      asserted to yield exactly one effective policy, without invoking\n      enforcement or telemetry.\n    decision_ids:\n      - D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Let the enforcement path pick the first matching policy.\n        reason: >-\n          Makes the effective policy an implicit side effect of iteration order\n          and leaves step 2 of the steel thread unprovable on its own.\n      - alternative: Allow resolution to return multiple candidate policies.\n        reason: >-\n          The blueprint requires exactly one effective policy per organization.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n      name: Policy resolution\n      owner: UNASSIGNED\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-ONE-EFFECTIVE-POLICY\n          observable_state: >-\n            For any organization and any set of validated policies, resolution\n            returns exactly one effective policy or an explicit no-policy result.\n          proof: >-\n            Resolution tests over overlapping, conflicting, and empty policy sets\n            assert single-valued, deterministic outcomes.\n          requires:\n            - validated versioned policy\n          produces:\n            - exactly one effective policy per organization\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-policy-resolution\n              title: Deterministic effective-policy resolution per organization\n              goal: >-\n                Resolve a validated policy set to exactly one effective policy\n                for an organization using declared precedence and tie-breaking.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Resolution over overlapping and conflicting policy sets returns\n                exactly one effective policy; an empty set returns an explicit\n                no-policy result; repeated resolution of the same input is\n                identical.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20261014-policy-schema\n              touches_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/policy_schema\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/resolution\n                - tests/ratelimit/resolution\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: An organization with several overlapping validated policies.\n                  when: Effective policy resolution runs.\n                  then: Exactly one effective policy is returned, chosen by declared precedence.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: An organization with no applicable policy.\n                  when: Effective policy resolution runs.\n                  then: An explicit no-policy result is returned rather than a default or an error.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Overlapping policy sets resolve to exactly one effective policy.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/resolution/run.sh overlapping\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Empty and non-matching sets return an explicit no-policy result.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/resolution/run.sh empty\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Resolution is deterministic across repeated and reordered input.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/resolution/run.sh deterministic\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Deriving precedence from provider metering or plan usage data.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Derive precedence only from declared policy fields.\n                - action: Persisting resolved policies to a chosen production store.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Production storage is not selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Resolve in memory over supplied validated policies.\n                - action: Returning a silent default policy when none applies.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Hides the no-policy case and makes the single-valued claim\n                    untestable.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Return an explicit no-policy result.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created resolution and test paths.\n              observability: Resolution records the chosen policy version and precedence reason.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - design\n                - build\n                - test\n\n  - id: SEAM-DECISION\n    name: Window accounting and denial decision\n    description: >-\n      Counting of requests within a window against the effective policy, the\n      allow or deny decision, the stable denial reason, and the matching\n      decision telemetry.\n    evidence:\n      - EV-BLUEPRINT\n    responsibility: >-\n      Own the per-window request count, the allow/deny outcome, the denial\n      reason contract, and emission of decision telemetry that matches the\n      returned decision.\n    consumes:\n      - exactly one effective policy per organization\n      - request event\n    produces:\n      - allow or deny decision\n      - stable denial reason\n      - decision telemetry event\n    owner: UNASSIGNED\n    independent_proof: >-\n      A 101-request sequence against a limit of 100 in one window asserts the\n      first 100 allowed and the 101st denied, and the emitted telemetry is\n      asserted to match the returned decision and reason.\n    decision_ids:\n      - D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP\n      - D-COUNTER-STORE\n      - D-METERING-BOUNDARY\n    rejected_alternatives:\n      - alternative: Derive the request count from provider usage metering.\n        reason: >-\n          Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope; reusing it would\n          make this seam a second consumer of a boundary the blueprint excludes.\n      - alternative: Emit telemetry from a separate asynchronous reconciliation job.\n        reason: >-\n          The blueprint requires the denial to emit matching telemetry, which a\n          decoupled job cannot prove within this thread.\n    swimlane:\n      id: LANE-DECISION\n      name: Decision and telemetry\n      owner: UNASSIGNED\n      legs:\n        - id: LEG-WINDOW-DENIAL\n          observable_state: >-\n            With an effective limit of 100 in a window, requests 1 through 100\n            are allowed and request 101 in the same window is denied.\n          proof: >-\n            Sequence test issuing 101 requests in one window asserting the\n            allow/deny boundary exactly at 101, and a window-rollover case.\n          requires:\n            - exactly one effective policy per organization\n          produces:\n            - allow or deny decision\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-window-decision\n              title: Window accounting and allow/deny decision at the policy limit\n              goal: >-\n                Count requests per organization within the policy window and deny\n                the first request that exceeds the effective limit.\n              done_condition: >-\n                Requests 1 through 100 are allowed and request 101 in the same\n                window is denied for a limit of 100; a request in the next window\n                is allowed again; counting goes through a port with no provider\n                metering dependency.\n              effort: M\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20261014-policy-resolution\n              touches_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/resolution\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/decision\n                - tests/ratelimit/decision\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: An organization with an effective limit of 100 in the current window.\n                  when: 101 requests are issued within that window.\n                  then: The first 100 are allowed and the 101st is denied.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: An organization that was denied in the previous window.\n                  when: A request arrives in the next window.\n                  then: The request is allowed because the window count has reset.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed in the same window.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/decision/run.sh boundary\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Window rollover resets the count and allows the next request.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/decision/run.sh rollover\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Counting depends only on the counter port, not provider metering.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/decision/run.sh counter-port-isolation\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Reading provider usage metering counters to decide allow or deny.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned and out of scope; the\n                    decision must not depend on it.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Count through the rate-limit counter port owned by this seam.\n                - action: Committing to a production counter store in this leaf.\n                  reason: >-\n                    D-COUNTER-STORE is unresolved and production storage is not\n                    selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Depend on a counter port and stop for the decision if a\n                    durable store is required to finish.\n                - action: Widening the denial to other quota or billing concerns.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Only the rate-limit decision is in scope for this thread.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Return a rate-limit decision and leave other quotas alone.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created decision and test paths.\n              observability: Each decision records organization, window, count, and outcome.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              shared_resources:\n                - ratelimit-counter-port\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\n        - id: LEG-DENIAL-TELEMETRY\n          observable_state: >-\n            A denial returns a stable reason identifier and emits exactly one\n            decision telemetry event whose fields match the returned decision.\n          proof: >-\n            Denial test asserting the reason identifier is stable across runs\n            and that the captured telemetry event matches the returned decision.\n          requires:\n            - allow or deny decision\n          produces:\n            - stable denial reason\n            - decision telemetry event\n          tasks:\n            - id: T-20261014-denial-telemetry\n              title: Stable denial reason and matching decision telemetry\n              goal: >-\n                Return a stable denial reason identifier and emit one decision\n                telemetry event that matches the returned decision.\n              done_condition: >-\n                A denial returns an enumerated, stable reason identifier;\n                exactly one telemetry event is emitted per decision; the event\n                fields match the returned decision and reason; telemetry carries\n                no provider metering fields.\n              effort: S\n              profile: standard\n              execution_backend: local\n              required_tools:\n                - bash\n              depends_on:\n                - T-20261014-window-decision\n              touches_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/decision\n              creates_paths:\n                - src/ratelimit/telemetry\n                - tests/ratelimit/telemetry\n              behavior:\n                - id: B-1\n                  given: A request denied for exceeding the effective limit.\n                  when: The decision is returned.\n                  then: The response carries an enumerated denial reason that is stable across runs.\n                - id: B-2\n                  given: Any allow or deny decision.\n                  when: The decision is returned.\n                  then: Exactly one telemetry event is emitted whose fields match the decision.\n              evals:\n                - id: eval_1\n                  description: Denial reason is enumerated and stable across repeated runs.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/telemetry/run.sh stable-reason\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                - id: eval_2\n                  description: Exactly one telemetry event per decision, matching the outcome.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/telemetry/run.sh event-match\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-2\n                - id: eval_3\n                  description: Telemetry carries no provider metering fields.\n                  bash: tests/ratelimit/telemetry/run.sh no-metering-fields\n                  verifies:\n                    - B-1\n                    - B-2\n              anti_patterns:\n                - action: Emitting telemetry into the provider usage metering pipeline.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Usage metering is provider-owned; decision telemetry must not\n                    become a metering feed.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Emit to the decision telemetry sink owned by this seam.\n                - action: Returning free-text denial messages.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Free text is not a stable reason and cannot be asserted.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Return an enumerated reason identifier.\n                - action: Selecting a production telemetry backend.\n                  reason: >-\n                    Deployment infrastructure is not selected by this plan.\n                  instead: >-\n                    Emit through a sink port captured in tests.\n              do_not_touch:\n                - provider usage metering surfaces\n                - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n              rollback: Remove the created telemetry and test paths.\n              observability: Decision telemetry is the observability surface for this thread.\n              execution_recipe: test-first\n              sdlc_stages:\n                - build\n                - test\n\nsteel_thread:\n  - LEG-SCHEMA-REJECTS-INVALID\n  - LEG-ONE-EFFECTIVE-POLICY\n  - LEG-WINDOW-DENIAL\n  - LEG-DENIAL-TELEMETRY\n\nobjections:\n  - id: OBJ-NO-SEAM-OWNER\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      No responsible owner is named for any in-scope seam or swimlane. Owners are\n      recorded as UNASSIGNED. The blueprint states only that usage metering is\n      provider-owned, which assigns nothing for policy, resolution, enforcement,\n      or telemetry. Ownership must be supplied by an explicit decision.\n  - id: OBJ-COUNTER-STORE-UNSELECTED\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      Steel thread step 3 requires counting 100 requests within a shared window,\n      but the blueprint declares production storage out of scope and unselected.\n      T-20261014-window-decision cannot reach a durable done condition until\n      D-COUNTER-STORE states whether the thread is proved against an in-process\n      reference counter behind a port or against a selected shared store.\n  - id: OBJ-NO-IMPLEMENTATION-SURFACE\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The repository contains no source tree, language, or runtime for the steel\n      thread. All touches_paths, creates_paths, and eval commands above are\n      proposed targets derived from the blueprint, not observed code. They\n      require confirmation against the real implementation repository before any\n      leaf is sealed.\n  - id: OBJ-REASON-CONTRACT-UNSPECIFIED\n    status: OPEN\n    summary: >-\n      The blueprint requires a stable denial reason but does not define the\n      stability contract or the telemetry sink. This plan proposes an enumerated\n      reason identifier and a sink port; both need confirmation.\n"}}}
