{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cg2hvWorvVpdym4HypwLz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Outcome: proposed plan authored, preparation **blocked** (not approved, not executed)\n\n**Plan draft:** `.taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml`\n**Initiative state:** `rate-limiting` at `DECOMPOSE=INTENT` — intake recorded (`tasks/.plans/rate-limiting/intake.md`), no delivery plan.\n\n### Proposed topology (3 seams → 4 capability legs → 4 leaves)\n\n| Thread step | Seam / leg | Leaf | Effort |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1. Schema rejects invalid limits/windows | `SEAM-POLICY-SCHEMA` → `LEG-SCHEMA-REJECTS-INVALID` | `T-20261014-policy-schema` | S |\n| 2. Exactly one effective policy per org | `SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION` → `LEG-ONE-EFFECTIVE-POLICY` | `T-20261014-policy-resolution` | S |\n| 3. Request 101 denied after 100 in window | `SEAM-DECISION` → `LEG-WINDOW-DENIAL` | `T-20261014-window-decision` | M |\n| 4. Stable reason + matching telemetry | `SEAM-DECISION` → `LEG-DENIAL-TELEMETRY` | `T-20261014-denial-telemetry` | S |\n\nSteps 3 and 4 share one seam because the denial reason and its telemetry are produced by the same decision, but they stay separate legs — each is independently assessable. The chain is sequential (`depends_on` 1→2→3→4): downstream proof still needs its declared dependencies.\n\n### Boundaries preserved as recorded, not reinterpreted\n- **`D-METERING-BOUNDARY` (accepted, owner: blueprint)** — provider-owned usage metering stays out. Carried into every leaf as an explicit anti-pattern and a `do_not_touch` entry; `LEG-WINDOW-DENIAL` counts through its own `ratelimit-counter-port`, and `eval_3` on both decision leaves asserts no provider-metering dependency and no metering fields in telemetry. The rejected alternative \"derive the count from provider usage metering\" is recorded with its reason.\n- **Storage/deployment not selected** — kept unselected. No store, runtime, or telemetry backend is chosen anywhere in the plan.\n\n### Blocker\n\n```\nDECOMPOSE=INVALID unaccepted_decision: Seam SEAM-POLICY-SCHEMA | SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION | SEAM-DECISION\n                  depend on decisions that are not accepted.\n```\n\nTwo unresolved product decisions, preserved in the recipe rather than cleared:\n\n1. **`D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP` (proposed, owner UNASSIGNED)** — blocks all three seams. The blueprint names ownership *only* for metering (\"provider-owned\"); it assigns no owner for policy, resolution, enforcement, or telemetry. Seam and swimlane owners are recorded `UNASSIGNED` rather than invented.\n2. **`D-COUNTER-STORE` (proposed, owner UNASSIGNED)** — additionally blocks `SEAM-DECISION`. Step 3 requires counting 100 requests in a shared window, while the blueprint declares production storage unselected. Unresolved: prove the thread against an in-process reference counter behind a port, or select a shared store first.\n\nAlso preserved as `OPEN` objections (not the validator's stopping point): no implementation surface exists in this repository — it holds only the fixture, so all `touches_paths`, `creates_paths`, and eval commands are proposed targets, not observed code — and the stability contract for the denial reason and the telemetry sink are unspecified.\n\n**Validation stopped at these blockers; checks beyond them (topology projection, leaf atomicity, write-surface conflicts) remain unproven.**\n\n### Smallest next action\n\nAsk the responsible human for **`D-SEAM-OWNERSHIP`** — one named owner per seam unblocks all three. `D-COUNTER-STORE` is then needed before `SEAM-DECISION` can prepare. With both recorded as `accepted` in the recipe, re-run:\n\n```bash\ntaskspec decompose prepare rate-limiting --recipe .taskspec/authoring-scratch/rate-limiting/rate-limiting-recipe.yaml\n```\n\nPer your instruction, I stopped at proposal: no `decompose review`, `compile`, `batch`, `gate --stamp`, or `accept` was run, nothing was committed, 